Three cuts to the zkVM inline allocation sequence (perf-26 objects, perf-49 arrays), ~1500 array and
~1900 object sites in the Nethermind guest:
- emitLoadImmediate gains the two-instruction form `lui rd, hi20; slli rd, rd, k` for constants that
  are a lui immediate shifted left (0xbfff0000 = 0x2fffc000 << 2), where the generic high32 + offset
  algorithm used lui + addiw + slli.
- The bump cell is addressed from a base: the next 16 KiB boundary at or above the cell when it is
  within imm12 reach (ZisK: cell 0xbffefff8, base 0xbfff0000, offsets -8 and -16), else the cell
  itself. The base loads in two instructions, and the heap floor is read through the same local with
  one ld instead of a second materialized constant (value numbering still sees an invariant load of a
  constant address, so it stays CSEd and hoisted).
- An array whose length is a constant gets no length guard, no size arithmetic and no widening: the
  payload size is folded at JIT time; a constant the helper would reject keeps the helper call.
Per allocation this is 3-4 fewer executed instructions (and ~5 for constant-length arrays), about
0.3% of the steps of block 25532480.

RISC-V64 zkVM: cheaper inline allocation - lui+slli constants, bump cell via base+imm12, constant lengths folded.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/emitriscv64.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/emitriscv64.cpp
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/emitriscv64.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/emitriscv64.cpp
@@ -1619,6 +1619,37 @@ int emitter::emitLoadImmediate(emitAttr size, regNumber reg, ssize_t imm)
         return 1;
     }
 
+    // Two-instruction form `lui rd, hi20; slli rd, rd, k` for imm == sext32(hi20 << 12) << k, k >= 1:
+    // a lui immediate shifted left. The generic high32 + offset algorithm below spends three
+    // instructions on such a value (lui, addiw, slli), e.g. on 0xbfff0000 = 0x2fffc000 << 2, the
+    // base the zkVM inline allocation addresses its bump cell from. A value that is itself a lui
+    // immediate (fits in 32 bits, low 12 bits zero) is left to that algorithm, which emits one.
+    if ((imm != 0) && !((imm == (int32_t)imm) && ((imm & 0xFFF) == 0)))
+    {
+        const int tz = BitOperations::TrailingZeroCount((uint64_t)imm);
+        for (int k = 1; k <= tz - 12; k++)
+        {
+            const int64_t v = (int64_t)imm >> k; // exact: the low k bits of imm are zero
+            if ((v == (int32_t)v) && ((v & 0xFFF) == 0))
+            {
+                if (doEmit)
+                {
+                    instrDescLoadImm* id = static_cast<instrDescLoadImm*>(emitNewInstrLoadImm(size, imm));
+                    id->idReg1(reg);
+                    id->ins[0]    = INS_lui;
+                    id->values[0] = (int32_t)(((uint64_t)v >> 12) & WordMask(20));
+                    id->ins[1]    = INS_slli;
+                    id->values[1] = k;
+                    id->idCodeSize(2 * 4);
+                    id->idIns(INS_slli);
+                    dispIns(id);
+                    appendToCurIG(id);
+                }
+                return 2;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+
     // The following algorithm works based on the following equation:
     // `imm = high32 + offset1` OR `imm = high32 - offset2`
     //
